# Commits and pull requests

When a task changes files in this repo, finish by committing and opening a pull request. Do this without asking first.

- Follow the repo git safety rules: no config changes, no force push, no skipped hooks, no amend unless the amend rules allow it.
- Do not commit secrets. `scripts/addons.local.json` stays untracked.
- Stage only files that belong to the task.
- Commit message: one or two sentences on why the change exists.
- Push the branch and open a pull request with `gh`. Return the PR URL.
- If the work is already on a feature branch with a PR, push the new commit to that branch instead of opening a second PR.
